venv
.venv
__pycache__/

# All corpus data is large - keep it out of git.
# (upload to Google Drive instead, and put the link in README.md)
#   raw/       source data: downloaded shards + combined manual corpus
#   interim/   per-stage cleaning checkpoints
#   processed/ final cleaned corpora, ready for tokenizer training
hindi/data/raw/
nepali/data/raw/
hindi/data/interim/
nepali/data/interim/
hindi/data/processed/
nepali/data/processed/
#   splits/    train/val/test jsonl + the tokenizer's training text (GBs)
#   bin/       uint16 token memmaps
# Note the "/*" rather than "/": git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT
# DIRECTORY is excluded, so "hindi/data/splits/" would make the "!" lines below
# dead letters. Excluding the directory's *contents* instead lets git descend
# and evaluate the negations, which is what keeps the small JSON manifests
# (split definitions, corpus metadata) tracked while the GB-scale data is not.
hindi/data/splits/*
!hindi/data/splits/combine_info.json
nepali/data/splits/*
!nepali/data/splits/combine_info.json
hindi/data/bin/*
!hindi/data/bin/meta.json
nepali/data/bin/*
!nepali/data/bin/meta.json

# NOTE: tokenizer/ is deliberately NOT ignored. An earlier version of this file
# excluded *.model on the assumption they were large binaries -- they are
# 0.4-1.1 MB, and the brief lists them as required deliverables ("Tokenizer
# model files (one per language)", plus "Separate tokenizers and vocabularies"
# in the final checklist). Both tokenizer/ directories together are ~6.6 MB, so
# the .model, .vocab, sweep_results.json and report.* files are all tracked.

# fastText language-ID model (131 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit).
# Downloaded once by hand, not a project artifact:
#   curl -L -o lid.176.bin https://dl.fbaipublicfiles.com/fasttext/supervised-models/lid.176.bin
lid.176.bin

# Belt-and-braces for the genuinely large formats, in case data ever lands
# outside the directories listed above. The tokenizer .model files are
# SentencePiece protobufs, not *.bin, so these patterns do not catch them.
*.bin
*.npy
*.jsonl.zst
*.partial

# ...but the corpus statistics are small JSON and worth tracking, so make sure
# nothing above accidentally excludes them.
!corpus_stats.json
